<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<chapter xml:id="ch-IV-multiple_integrals" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>Multiple Integrals</title>

  <introduction>
  <p>
    Multiple integrals: specifically double integrals (<m>\iint_{R}</m>) over
        two-dimensional regions and triple integrals (<m>\iiint_{E}</m>) over
        three-dimensional solids generalize definite integration to functions of
        several variables. Their core purpose is to accumulate a quantity that varies across space by
        breaking a region or solid into tiny elements (<m>dA</m> or <m>dV</m>),
        multiplying the local density or value by the element size, and summing over the
        entire domain.
  </p>
  
  </introduction>

